# menu-walk-port -- the Dolphin reference walk, on the port's own clock.
#
# ref/movies/menu-walk.play is the reference schedule converted directly, and
# it does not replay here: its frame numbers are the console's, and the two
# sides do not agree on absolute frames.  The console spends 186 frames on the
# cold-boot logos (a *wall-clock* wait -- ref/notes.md 2) and then 4,195 frames
# on the opening THP movie; the port skips the movie outright (M8) and loads
# off a local disc image, so it arrives at the title around frame 700 with the
# console's START pulses at 380/430/480 long spent.
#
# So this is the same walk with the same shape -- accept the title, then A
# every 90 frames through the file select, the new-file scene and the Party
# Mode prompts -- rebased on where the port actually is.  The START pulses are
# repeated rather than pinned for the same reason ref/movies/menu-walk.txt
# repeats its three: the exact frame the title starts taking input is not
# worth pinning down, and an extra START on the title screen is harmless.

# Accept the title.
at 700 6 START
at 750 6 START
at 800 6 START
at 850 6 START
at 900 6 START
at 950 6 START
at 1000 6 START
at 1050 6 START
at 1100 6 START

# Walk forward with A: file select, the new-file scene, the Party Mode prompts,
# character select and the board settings.
at 1160 6 A
at 1250 6 A
at 1340 6 A
at 1430 6 A
at 1520 6 A
at 1610 6 A
at 1700 6 A
at 1790 6 A
at 1880 6 A
at 1970 6 A
at 2060 6 A
at 2150 6 A
at 2240 6 A
at 2330 6 A
at 2420 6 A
at 2510 6 A
at 2600 6 A
at 2690 6 A
at 2780 6 A
at 2870 6 A
at 2960 6 A
at 3050 6 A
at 3140 6 A
at 3230 6 A
at 3320 6 A
at 3410 6 A
at 3500 6 A
at 3590 6 A
at 3680 6 A
at 3770 6 A
at 3860 6 A
at 3950 6 A
at 4040 6 A
at 4130 6 A
at 4220 6 A
at 4310 6 A
at 4400 6 A
at 4490 6 A
at 4580 6 A
at 4670 6 A
at 4760 6 A
at 4850 6 A
at 4940 6 A
